                "path": "../manifest.json"
              },
              "detail": "Global mosaic",
              "summary": "Source detail ranges from 400 m to 60 km per pixel. Photographed shadows and seams remain; the gray grid marks missing data."
            },
            {
              "id": "enhanced",
              "label": "Galileo color",
              "description": "Published NASA/JPL/DLR processed color from Galileo in May 2001, registered to the controlled USGS map. About 8 km per source pixel near the disk center; detail becomes coarser toward the edge. This is display color, not calibrated I/F or albedo. Only views within 65° of the surface normal are retained; gray grid marks the rest of the globe. Photographed shading and color fringes remain; added globe lighting is approximate.",
              "title": "Processed color mosaic",
              "thumbnail": "/scenes/callisto/callisto-enhanced-thumbnail.webp",
              "surface": "callisto-enhanced-surface@2x.webp",
              "poles": "callisto-enhanced-poles@2x.webp",
              "source": {
                "id": "galileo-pia03456-registered-color",
                "path": "../manifest.json"
              },
              "detail": "Partial processed color",
              "summary": "May 2001 Galileo color over about 29% of the globe. Gray grid: unseen or withheld. Processed display colors, not albedo.",
              "falseColor": true,
              "legend": {
                "kind": "categories",
                "title": "Coverage",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "label": "Color",
